    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Championships: NBA and WNBA eras\"\n---\n\n\n\n\n::: {.callout-important appearance=\"simple\"}\n## Why the time windows differ\n- **NBA section:** every NBA season we have, **2003-04 to 2025-26** (23 seasons, 23 champions).\n- **WNBA section:** every WNBA season we have, **2009 to 2026** (18 seasons, 18 champions).\n- **NBA vs WNBA comparison:** only the **shared window, 2009 to 2026**, so differences between the leagues are not\n  differences between years.\n- **Models that learn from champions use all of each league's seasons.** There is only one champion per season, so a\n  10-season window would leave just 10 champions to learn from, too few to test a title model. More seasons also\n  give the era-drift results their meaning (e.g. the NBA's mid-2000s defense-led champions).\n- Some measurements start later in both leagues (drive and pull-up tags: NBA 2017-18, WNBA 2019) and are used only where they exist.\n- **Shot zones are calibrated by season.** ESPN's recorded shot positions drift between eras, most visibly in the\n  WNBA's 2020 bubble season, so the rim zone is anchored to where layups are recorded each season (Data page).\n:::\n\n\n\n::: {#takeaways .cell execution_count=2}\n\n::: {.callout-note appearance=\"simple\"}\n## Takeaways\n- **NBA playoffs punish threes and rim attempts.** Points per three fell in the playoffs in\n  100% of 23 seasons (-0.040 per shot);\n  rim attempts in 91% (-0.034). Mid-range shots held up best.\n- **WNBA playoffs:** no shot zone shows a reliable playoff change (every 95% interval includes zero); with 8-12 playoff teams a year the sample is small.\n- **The WNBA is about 6 years behind the NBA on the three-point shift.** In 2026,\n  37% of WNBA shots were threes.\n- **Recent champions vs their own league (2022-26):** WNBA champions took +5.3 points more of their shots from three and\n  -6.3 at the rim; NBA champions +2.3 and -0.7.\n:::\n\n:::\n\n\n# NBA (2003-04 to 2025-26)\n\n## NBA: which shots survive the playoffs?\n\nPoints per shot in the playoffs minus the regular season, by zone. Below zero = the shot got worse in the playoffs.\n\n\n```{=html}\n<div>                            <div id=\"b0f374d8-a389-4241-9d38-60ee3ff339bd\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:360px; width:100%;\"></div>            <script type=\"text/javascript\">                                    window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};                                    if (document.getElementById(\"b0f374d8-a389-4241-9d38-60ee3ff339bd\")) {                    Plotly.newPlot(                        \"b0f374d8-a389-4241-9d38-60ee3ff339bd\",                        [{\"hovertemplate\":\"three: %{y:+.3f}\\u003cextra\\u003e\\u003c\\u002fextra\\u003e\",\"line\":{\"color\":\"#2a78d6\",\"width\":2},\"marker\":{\"color\":\"#2a78d6\",\"size\":6},\"mode\":\"lines+markers\",\"name\":\"three\",\"x\":[2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025,2026],\"y\":[-0.0778595266990289,-0.0062231655063593,-0.0345380454604726,-0.0381514556250819,-0.054391828595995,-0.0391250686180315,-0.0347441075086192,-0.0607358864294551,-0.0676478421134136,-0.0653892729174097,-0.0267470952821231,-0.0474971643506758,-0.0091358703524528,-0.0126769652960538,-0.0424248550551047,-0.0499280520400404,-0.0052648518869189,-0.039954246244257,-0.0134845021877736,-0.0489306141483829,-0.0701437533123461,-0.0412735294431552,-0.0405225622650589],\"type\":\"scatter\"},{\"hovertemplate\":\"rim: %{y:+.3f}\\u003cextra\\u003e\\u003c\\u002fextra\\u003e\",\"line\":{\"color\":\"#eb6834\",\"width\":2},\"marker\":{\"color\":\"#eb6834\",\"size\":6},\"mode\":\"lines+markers\",\"name\":\"rim\",\"x\":[2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025,2026],\"y\":[-0.0455458217953663,-0.0365966855992825,0.0293531846448011,-0.0392962301417827,-0.0587598181249617,-0.0406974415106016,-0.052522780263958,-0.10417682276944